<ol>
<li>OTHER FEES Late payments: up to $35. Cash advance fee: 3% of the transaction amount (Min $2, Max $50). Foreign currency transaction: 3% of the transaction in USD.</li>
</ol>
<p>X. DEFAULT RATE No penalty rate applies. Any changes will be notified per legal requirements.</p>
<ol>
<li>MONTHLY STATEMENT The statement will show prior balance, payments, credits, debits, purchases, cash advances, interest charges, APR, new balance, minimum payment, and due date. Errors must be reported within 60 days.</li>
<li>XII.LOST OR STOLEN CARD Report immediately to 1-877-929-FACE (3223) or 787-705-7642. Liability is limited to $50 if reported promptly.</li>
<li>XIII.CARD DENIAL The Bank may decline purchases or cash advances even if credit is available. Suspicious activity may result in temporary suspension.</li>
<li>XIV.JOINT ACCOUNTS Joint cardholders are jointly liable. The Bank may require all cardholders’ signatures for certain instructions.</li>
<li>XV.DEFAULT Failure to pay, bankruptcy, or exceeding credit limit without authorization constitutes default. The Bank may collect the entire balance plus legal fees.</li>
<li>XVI.AMENDMENTS Interest rates and terms may change with 45 days’ notice if adverse to the Cardholder.</li>
<li>XVII.MISCELLANEOUS Omission by the Bank to exercise rights does not constitute waiver. Invalid clauses do not affect the remainder of the agreement.</li>
<li>XVIII.BILLING RIGHTS You have rights under the Fair Credit Billing Act to dispute billing errors. Report errors within 60 days.</li>
<li>XIX.AFTER WRITTEN NOTICE The Bank must acknowledge your dispute within 30 days and resolve within 90 days.</li>
<li>XX.SPECIAL RULES FOR PURCHASES You may withhold payment for disputed goods/services if you attempted to resolve in good faith with the seller and meet other criteria.</li>
<li>XXI.COLLATERAL The Cardholder agrees to provide a Certificate of Deposit as collateral for all debts incurred on the card. The Bank may liquidate the CD in case of default after 90 days.</li>
</ol>
